+// Fast buffer-pointer resolution for the binary-arith fast path.
+//
+// ADD/SUB/MUL are pure elementwise: their inputs and output are plain
+// BufferPool buffer indices. Codegen guarantees the indices are in-range
+// (0..MAX_BUFFERS-1) and BufferPool::ensure_capacity() armed every slab the
+// program references at load time (slabs are never freed), so the
+// bounds-check and null-slab check in BufferPool::get() are dead weight on
+// this hot path. Resolving the pointer directly yields the *identical*
+// address (same slab, same row); SLAB_BUFFERS is a power of two, so the
+// / and % below compile to a shift and a mask. Bit-for-bit the same buffer.
+inline float* buf_ptr(BufferPool* bp, std::uint16_t idx) noexcept {
+    return bp->slabs_[idx / SLAB_BUFFERS]->get()->data[idx % SLAB_BUFFERS].data();
+}
+
